        16,
        1210.5
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": "7",
        "width": 2016,
        "height": 472.75,
        "content": "## Weekly performance digest\n\nOn Monday evening, the workflow summarizes this week’s logged leads with DeepSeek and emails the owner a digest, followed by a Telegram alert."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sn-main-19622",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -662,
        -393.75
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 590,
        "height": 660,
        "content": "## Dental clinic audit outreach\n\n### How it works\n1. Every Monday morning, SerpAPI searches Google Maps for dental clinics in your target city.\n2. The workflow normalizes results, keeps clinics with a phone number and website, then Hunter finds business emails. Incomplete records go to the Skipped sheet.\n3. DeepSeek scores qualified clinics and writes a personalized audit offer. Gmail sends it, Google Sheets logs the lead, and Telegram alerts your team.\n4. On Monday evening, the workflow summarizes that week’s logged leads with DeepSeek and sends the owner a digest by Gmail and Telegram.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Connect SerpAPI, Hunter, Gmail, Google Sheets, and Telegram credentials.\n- [ ] Self-host n8n and install the SerpAPI community node for Google Maps search.\n- [ ] Create a Google Sheet with Leads and Skipped tabs, then add its ID to each Sheets node.\n- [ ] Replace the Telegram chat ID and digest recipient email address.\n\n### Customization\nChange the target city, search query, sender name, offer details, or delivery channels in Prospecting Config before activating the workflow."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
